<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kawar people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kawar, also written Kanwar, are an Adivasi people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, living mainly in the northern districts such as Korba, Surguja, Bilaspur and Jashpur. Traditionally settled farmers, they claim descent from the Kauravas of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a> and speak Chhattisgarhi. They are one of the larger <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheduled-tribes">Scheduled Tribes</a> of the state.</p></div>
